WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.378 --> 00:00:03.700
- A lot of people have
their own different niche,

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.196
and you know, you don't have to be

00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:06.928
a super lyricist or a storyteller.

00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:08.659
It could just be the energy you bring.

00:00:08.659 --> 00:00:10.480
People don't like to look
themselves in the mirror.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.400
That's the hardest thing to do, you know,

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.993
is to critique yourself.

00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:17.080
When I started doing music,
at first I was selfish.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.276
Doing music, I mean, that I like.

00:00:19.276 --> 00:00:21.387
You want the flashy
things until, you know,

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.259
you grow older, you know, as an adult.

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:25.956
And you be able to understand
yourself a little bit more.

00:00:25.956 --> 00:00:28.899
- He's an American rapper
from Compton, California.

00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:32.038
His major label debut
was in October of 2012,

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:33.251
to critical success.

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.702
Time named him one of the hundred

00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:37.839
most influential people
in the world in 2016.

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:39.707
He's Kendrick Lamar and here is my take

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:41.799
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:42.742
As you guys watch and listen,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.066
if you hear something that Kendrick says

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.023
that you really love,
make sure to leave it

00:00:46.023 --> 00:00:48.083
in the comments below with quotation marks

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:50.366
so we can keep track of what impacted you.

00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:53.327
(logo swooshing)

00:00:53.327 --> 00:00:55.320
- It's a whole world out there, man,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.631
that believes in what you
can do and what you can say

00:00:58.631 --> 00:01:00.455
and the energy you bring, you know.

00:01:00.455 --> 00:01:02.987
I'm not even just justifying myself.

00:01:02.987 --> 00:01:06.446
A lot of people have
their own different niche,

00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:07.902
and you know, you don't have to be

00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:09.632
a super lyricist or a storyteller.

00:01:09.632 --> 00:01:11.499
It could just be the energy you bring.

00:01:11.499 --> 00:01:13.232
Know what I'm saying,
they believe in that.

00:01:13.232 --> 00:01:14.310
But the moment they feel like

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.275
you don't believe in that no more

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:17.814
and you just going with the next trend,

00:01:17.814 --> 00:01:21.884
whether it's 808s or whether
it's a up-tempo or slow-tempo--

00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:23.243
- [Man] Autotune or whatever.

00:01:23.243 --> 00:01:24.076
- Exactly.

00:01:24.076 --> 00:01:25.814
They don't believe in
you no more, you know,

00:01:25.814 --> 00:01:27.358
the culture don't believe in you no more.

00:01:27.358 --> 00:01:31.387
So stand behind what you do and you know,

00:01:31.387 --> 00:01:33.287
the world is going to move by it.

00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:34.925
And that's exactly how I look at it.

00:01:34.925 --> 00:01:36.588
People don't like to look
at themselves in the mirror.

00:01:36.588 --> 00:01:38.646
That's the hardest thing to do, you know,

00:01:38.646 --> 00:01:40.704
is to critique yourself

00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:43.121
rather than point the finger.

00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:46.253
Everybody hates change.

00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:49.011
So to actually do that and say

00:01:49.011 --> 00:01:50.936
"I'm wrong in a lot of areas."

00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:52.382
I look at myself in the
mirror and I'm saying,

00:01:52.382 --> 00:01:53.783
"I'm wrong in a lot of areas,"

00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:56.172
that takes a lot of willpower,
you dig what I'm saying?

00:01:56.172 --> 00:01:58.357
So it started with self first.

00:01:58.357 --> 00:02:00.836
The nickname, that been
acquired since I was a kid,

00:02:00.836 --> 00:02:02.292
just being in the neighborhood.

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:04.070
Something given to me by just my homeboys

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.301
growing up in Compton, so that
name will always be there.

00:02:07.301 --> 00:02:08.175
I'll go back to the city now

00:02:08.175 --> 00:02:09.809
and they don't call me Kendrick.

00:02:09.809 --> 00:02:11.865
I just felt like it was
a time for me to grow,

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.250
you know, not only as a
artist but as a person.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.199
I want the world to know me for who I am.

00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:20.175
And I just sit back and
reflect on why Tupac

00:02:20.175 --> 00:02:21.151
is one of the greatest,

00:02:21.151 --> 00:02:23.395
why BIG's one of the greatest, why Jay is.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:25.553
Because the people felt
like they had a connection,

00:02:25.553 --> 00:02:29.576
it wasn't just a facade that
you seen on stage or on TV.

00:02:29.576 --> 00:02:32.338
People actually felt like it was a part

00:02:32.338 --> 00:02:34.112
of what you was going through

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:37.618
and your worries and just life in general.

00:02:37.618 --> 00:02:40.010
You know, I said what
better way to start that

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.144
rather than giving them my real name,

00:02:43.144 --> 00:02:45.199
letting them know who I am as a person.

00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:47.622
My songs are personal, I do
try to make it universal.

00:02:47.622 --> 00:02:49.771
It took me a long time to figure that out,

00:02:49.771 --> 00:02:52.163
and not stay just in that one box.

00:02:52.163 --> 00:02:53.840
Because now I know the world is listening.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.881
When I started doing music,
at first I was selfish.

00:02:56.881 --> 00:02:59.631
Doing music, I mean, that I like.

00:03:01.749 --> 00:03:03.469
I got a whole community behind me now,

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:04.757
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:04.757 --> 00:03:06.815
So it's more of a responsibility

00:03:06.815 --> 00:03:10.023
'cause they banking on me
to have some positive light.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.711
You know what I mean, the city of Compton,

00:03:11.711 --> 00:03:13.738
there's always been a
negative stigma there.

00:03:13.738 --> 00:03:14.957
So I'm at a point now

00:03:14.957 --> 00:03:16.926
where I can walk through any neighborhood

00:03:16.926 --> 00:03:19.401
and they'll be like, "Yo
nigga, you better go.

00:03:19.401 --> 00:03:23.569
You better do it for us
because at the end of the day,

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.342
we going to be locked up."

00:03:25.342 --> 00:03:27.332
They're locked up in the
penitentiary calling me and saying,

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:29.858
"Yo, I need you to look
out for my little son

00:03:29.858 --> 00:03:33.274
or my nephew through your
music," dig what I'm saying?

00:03:33.274 --> 00:03:34.491
That's a responsibility I have

00:03:34.491 --> 00:03:35.890
and that's what keeps me humble, man.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.045
That and just life in
general, and my family.

00:03:38.045 --> 00:03:40.895
I'm the oldest of four, you know,

00:03:40.895 --> 00:03:42.161
so I got to make a for them

00:03:42.161 --> 00:03:43.568
and make a positive life for them.

00:03:43.568 --> 00:03:45.859
My little brother's 17 now and
he's in the city of Compton.

00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:49.618
He might go through the same
steps and mistakes that I made.

00:03:49.618 --> 00:03:53.931
So that's what really humbles
me and keeps my head level.

00:03:53.931 --> 00:03:57.439
I think some of my best
advice recently came from Dre,

00:03:57.439 --> 00:03:59.541
is to keep the passion for the music.

00:03:59.541 --> 00:04:00.618
You know, always keep that

00:04:00.618 --> 00:04:02.585
because so many people lose passion

00:04:02.585 --> 00:04:04.592
and everything's starting
to be about a dollar

00:04:04.592 --> 00:04:07.121
and that's when you know the
value of the music goes down.

00:04:07.121 --> 00:04:09.454
When I was listening to NWA,

00:04:11.378 --> 00:04:13.044
anything that I did in the streets,

00:04:13.044 --> 00:04:16.407
it wasn't from NWA, it was because

00:04:16.407 --> 00:04:20.434
my cousins was doing it,
you know, my uncle was.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:24.410
A song really didn't,
the songs that they had

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.160
was just autobiography
of what I seen anyway.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.969
So for me, personally, knowing
how kids react to music,

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:39.161
that's why I tend to always
have the reasoning behind it.

00:04:39.161 --> 00:04:41.265
It's still gangsta rap, it's still harsh.

00:04:41.265 --> 00:04:43.837
And some parents may not want their kids

00:04:43.837 --> 00:04:45.053
to listen to some records.

00:04:45.053 --> 00:04:46.974
Not all records, but some records.

00:04:46.974 --> 00:04:50.060
But at the same time, when
I do do these records,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.903
it's a sort of responsibility of giving,

00:04:53.903 --> 00:04:57.504
like I said, the happenings behind it.

00:04:57.504 --> 00:04:58.861
Yeah, you can go kill somebody,

00:04:58.861 --> 00:05:00.500
I'm going to talk about killing somebody,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:04.523
but I'm not going to talk
about it without saying

00:05:04.523 --> 00:05:08.171
that you're risking your
life for 25 years times four

00:05:08.171 --> 00:05:11.088
in the state correctional facility.

00:05:11.963 --> 00:05:15.096
It's not just doing it for fun,

00:05:15.096 --> 00:05:17.483
with bottles and women around me.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:21.185
I'm talking about it
with cuffs and chains,

00:05:21.185 --> 00:05:23.288
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:26.140
Any kid that's listening to it,

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.810
you're going to have a precaution.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.255
That's the realities that be.

00:05:30.255 --> 00:05:31.990
I'm just going to continue to give people

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.985
what I know, what I want to know,

00:05:34.985 --> 00:05:37.795
what they don't know, and
what we all can learn.

00:05:37.795 --> 00:05:42.283
The reason why we're on earth
today, you, me, him, her,

00:05:42.283 --> 00:05:45.116
all these different walks of life,

00:05:47.484 --> 00:05:50.138
is all a test, it's
almost like an experiment,

00:05:50.138 --> 00:05:51.555
God's experiment.

00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:56.358
When are we going to understand

00:05:56.358 --> 00:05:59.108
that we are put on earth to love?

00:06:00.806 --> 00:06:02.485
That's all it's about.

00:06:02.485 --> 00:06:04.456
Everybody wants to figure
out how complicated

00:06:04.456 --> 00:06:06.743
life is and break it down.

00:06:06.743 --> 00:06:08.431
This is what I truly think.

00:06:08.431 --> 00:06:10.014
I really think that

00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:15.398
it's going to keep going on.

00:06:15.398 --> 00:06:16.710
War going to keep going on,

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.094
frustration going to keep going
on, anger will keep going on,

00:06:19.094 --> 00:06:22.977
'til we finally go back
down to the simplest word.

00:06:22.977 --> 00:06:23.810
Love.

00:06:24.661 --> 00:06:26.578
And when God sees that,

00:06:31.472 --> 00:06:33.844
then we have an answer.

00:06:33.844 --> 00:06:36.372
But until then it's going to be warfare.

00:06:36.372 --> 00:06:38.335
You want the flashy
things until, you know,

00:06:38.335 --> 00:06:40.212
you grow older, you know, as an adult.

00:06:40.212 --> 00:06:42.923
And you be able to understand
yourself a little bit more.

00:06:42.923 --> 00:06:45.307
I learned that them things
didn't make me happy.

00:06:45.307 --> 00:06:49.446
I learned that money really don't make me,

00:06:49.446 --> 00:06:51.196
I'm learning that now, you know.

00:06:51.196 --> 00:06:55.311
That's not really my peace
of mind, having money.

00:06:55.311 --> 00:06:57.536
That's something I learned this
year and years before that.

00:06:57.536 --> 00:06:59.646
And learned that jewelry
and all that stuff

00:06:59.646 --> 00:07:00.928
won't really make me happy.

00:07:00.928 --> 00:07:04.295
And when you learn that,
you'll be able to grow,

00:07:04.295 --> 00:07:06.357
grow more as a person.

00:07:06.357 --> 00:07:08.228
What makes me happy is
really challenging myself

00:07:08.228 --> 00:07:11.646
and knowing that I defeated my last goal

00:07:11.646 --> 00:07:15.102
and took myself to the next
level, was a better person.

00:07:15.102 --> 00:07:16.602
- It was for real, I think.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.704
They called you "The Black Dylan."

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:19.921
- That was crazy.

00:07:19.921 --> 00:07:22.589
- Yeah, 'cause Dylan was prolific,

00:07:22.589 --> 00:07:24.320
and I'm sure that's
where he's coming from.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.167
- Yeah, definitely.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.604
Always said, man, if I'm going to do this

00:07:26.604 --> 00:07:28.009
I'm going to say something.

00:07:28.009 --> 00:07:30.112
I'm not just going to
rap a bunch of verses.

00:07:30.112 --> 00:07:34.112
(audience applauding, cheering)

00:07:35.531 --> 00:07:37.715
That's what Dylan, you
know, he's a legend.

00:07:37.715 --> 00:07:39.692
And he said something,
he voiced his opinion.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:43.196
And the world gravitated towards it

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:44.779
and I want to do that with music.

00:07:44.779 --> 00:07:46.184
- [Reporter] This young, dedicated artist

00:07:46.184 --> 00:07:49.360
can't help but reflect on
those who once doubted him.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.329
- [Kendrick] They never said
I wasn't talented enough.

00:07:51.329 --> 00:07:53.576
They'll say something like,
"The industry is shady.

00:07:53.576 --> 00:07:54.975
You don't need to be doing this."

00:07:54.975 --> 00:07:57.085
I respect their opinions
but at the end of the day

00:07:57.085 --> 00:07:59.097
I have to follow my heart
and that's what I want to do.

00:07:59.097 --> 00:08:01.341
It was a passion, I couldn't shake it.

00:08:01.341 --> 00:08:03.259
And I be hurt now if
I didn't stick with it

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:05.200
because it'll always be on my head.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.910
